<Plain
	title="About · today.duinlab.nl"
	description="What today.duinlab.nl is, what it keeps, where its facts come from, and its code."
>
	<Fragment slot="title">About this page</Fragment>

	<p>
		A daily page for two of us in The Hague, open to anyone: one picture, a few facts, a word, a quiz and ten
		games. It changes at midnight, Amsterdam time.
	</p>

	<h2>Privacy</h2>
	<p>
		No cookies, no analytics. Your played games, streaks and quiz answers stay in this browser's local storage
		(<code>today.games.v1</code>, <code>today.quiz.v1</code>) and are never sent anywhere. Clear the site's data
		to remove them.
	</p>
	<p>
		A Cloudflare Worker serves the page. Cloudflare keeps request logs for a few days: the address asked for,
		the time, and connection details such as your IP address. I only read them to trace a fault.
	</p>

	<h2>Accessibility</h2>
	<p>
		The aim is WCAG 2.2 AA. Text contrast holds in every sky, games and answers are at least 44 pixels tall,
		keyboard focus is visible, motion stops when your system asks for less, and the page reads in full without
		JavaScript. Every change runs an axe check. If something gets in your way,
		<a href="https://github.com/simonvanlierde/duinlab-today/issues">open an issue</a>.
	</p>

	<h2>Sources</h2>
	<p>
		Each fact links to where it came from: Wikipedia, Wiktionary, NASA APOD, The Metropolitan Museum of Art,
		Open Trivia DB (CC BY-SA 4.0), ZenQuotes, and <a href="https://open-meteo.com/">Open-Meteo</a> for the
		weather. The weather line opens
		<a href="https://www.buienradar.nl/weer/den-haag/nl/2747373">Buienradar</a>. The sky is worked out from
		the sun's position over The Hague, in your browser.
	</p>

	<h2>Code</h2>
	<p>
		<a href="https://github.com/simonvanlierde/duinlab-today">github.com/simonvanlierde/duinlab-today</a>, MIT
		licence. The day's data is at <a href="/today.json">today.json</a>.
	</p>
</Plain>
